# Experimental `project-basic` Workflow — Release Requirements

Initiative: `7ca3d0c1-a55d-4307-a7e2-ddc8ec4d3582`  
Pack / workflow: `forge-framework-change` 0.1.0 / `framework-change` 0.1.0  
Step: `scope` — required output role `release-requirements`

This defines the successor’s acceptance target. It is not a check, evidence packet, verification, or owner acceptance. Its companion is [change-scope.md](change-scope.md).

## Machine-verifiable requirements

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| M1 | `project-basic@0.1.0` safe-loads and validates as a bundled, data-only pack with exactly the seven declared phases and standard existing transitions. |
| M2 | Every phase has the declared inputs/outputs, supported actor set, check requirement, owner acceptance requirement, and phase guidance; all four explanation profiles are present. |
| M3 | Pack interview guidance is digest-bound and includes vision, first milestone, risk/constraint, and learning-path coverage. Guidance changes no authority, transition, condition, or acceptance behavior. |
| M4 | The pack declares exactly eleven non-executable UTF-8 templates, excludes `created-work`, and validates template inventory, available list/show, and locked list/show behavior. |
| M5 | The research template supports a documented `no new research needed` result naming considered materials, sufficiency basis, remaining uncertainty, and owner review. |
| M6 | The evaluation template explicitly binds exact `created-work` and `acceptance-criteria` revision IDs and digests; it distinguishes pass/fail/skip findings, limitations, and a non-automatic rework recommendation. |
| M7 | Revising `created-work` invalidates dependent work and permits native `begin` rework; no `revise` transition or automatic evaluation transition exists. |
| M8 | Existing `software-basic@0.6.0`, `research-basic@0.4.0`, repository-local pack identities, and archived locks retain their recorded digests. |
| M9 | Version-contract, installation matrix, version-consistency, CLI discovery, installed-wheel smoke, example smoke, and tests recognize sorted bundled inventory `project-basic`, `research-basic`, `software-basic`. |
| M10 | Documentation provides one canonical project-companion statement and correctly routes project selection without changing the CLI default. It describes guidance as advisory and preserves owner-gate boundaries. |
| M11 | The dogfood guide contains five owner-observed scenario protocols and no claimed scenario outcome. |
| M12 | Current-source validation states that Production-v1 candidate artifacts are historical and not proof for changed source bytes; historical candidate manifests, hashes, and release records remain unchanged. |
| M13 | Focused pack/lifecycle/distribution tests, version consistency, static example smoke, formatting, lint, type checks, and the appropriate full local test suite pass on the same revision. Any Windows environmental limitation is rerun with a short writable pytest base before classification. |

## Owner-observed follow-up

The implementation delivers the dogfood guide, not pretend dogfood evidence. Each later owner-observed run should record the exact project/basic pack revision, agent and prompt, scenario, context supplied, workflow recommendation, vision capture, question quality, teaching, delegation, confusion/friction, comparison with ordinary chat, limitations, and owner verdict.

Scenarios are: beginner game, scientific/evidence project, physical-making project, creative writing/song project, and a small clear software change. The software scenario should document why `software-basic` is the better fit when vision and context already exist.

